Z||000000||filthyscarecrow||11-07-2001||01:33 AM||||just how much extra flow can you get out of the fuel system by playing with fuel pressure? is it possible to run low amounts of boost with stock injectors if you mess with the regulator? (i'm not going to, but i'm trying to get an idea of flow here.) i saw a thread on making an adjustable regulator, how much extra fuel delivery could this result in with a stock fuel pump? 10% gain? 20% <BR>if anyone knows anything, i'd really appreciate the help. thanks... <P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||fierospeeder||11-07-2001||03:06 AM||||you can pull the vacuum line off the pressure regulator and you get about an extra 5-10 psi at idle.  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Alex4mula||11-07-2001||09:49 AM||||That's the same 5-10 you get at WOT, i.e. does nothing. Stock injectors can support a normal boost turbo, NOS, etc. I haven't heard that Design One turbo kit replaces injectors, so no need. <P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red-Original Owner & White-1/94 with PM (:||||reg||1
